{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory correctly prioritized the right breast BI-RADS 4B lesion, distinguished it from thyroid and lung follow-up issues, repeatedly redirected the patient to breast surgery/pathology review, and gave practical red-flag and follow-up guidance. However, once the patient was clearly preparing for surgery, the doctor did not visibly remind the patient to ensure the offline surgical/anesthesia team knew the chronic hepatitis B/liver-function and coagulation/anticoagulant context required by RC5; this is a minor/moderate responsibility-chain omission and caps the grade at 2. Later high-order strengths and extensive follow-up cannot erase that in-chain error.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00785",
        "explanation": "The doctor left a safe breast-follow-up plan and red-flag threshold near the end of the observable trajectory.",
        "quote": "按乳腺外科给你的随访时间走"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The bounded episode remains safely open rather than fully closed because the final patient message asked a residual thyroid/lung prioritization question without a subsequent doctor response. The main breast-pathology and wound-care plan was still executable and traceable, and the unanswered issue was a lower-priority allowed residual risk rather than an unsafe termination.",
    "label": "valid_open",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00221",
        "explanation": "The doctor converted the immediate post-discharge situation into a concrete sequence of wound care, pathology tracking, and breast follow-up.",
        "quote": "先养伤口；盯住3-5个工作日的石蜡病理"
      }
    ],
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
        "explanation": "The doctor correctly set the diagnostic priority on the BI-RADS 4B breast lesion rather than the thyroid or lung findings.",
        "quote": "现在最该先处理的是右侧乳腺 BI-RADS 4B"
      }
    ],
    "continuity_memory_focus": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00585",
        "explanation": "The doctor maintained continuity across wound care, pathology timing, and breast surgery follow-up.",
        "quote": "周五先换药看伤口，下周二带病理去乳腺外科复诊"
      }
    ],
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00482",
        "explanation": "The doctor recognized medication and postoperative safety risks and warned against unsafe analgesic stacking.",
        "quote": "不要自己再叠加别的止痛药"
      }
    ],
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00116",
        "explanation": "The doctor adapted communication into a short script the patient could show or read to the surgical team.",
        "quote": "可以直接念的"
      }
    ]
  },
  "dimension_ratings": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": "partial",
    "clinical_reasoning_direction": "excellent",
    "continuity_memory_focus": "excellent",
    "medical_safety_risk_recognition": "partial",
    "patient_family_realworld_adaptation": "excellent"
  },
  "high_order_assessment": [
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00055",
          "explanation": "The doctor repaired confusion between direct excision, frozen section, and cancer diagnosis rather than treating the surgery plan as proof of cancer.",
          "quote": "不等于已经确诊癌"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00075",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave a targeted consent/checklist strategy for the frozen-section branch and possible intraoperative escalation.",
          "quote": "术中最可能出现的两三种情况"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The patient was confused by observation, excision, and frozen-section language; the doctor actively explained the distinction and integrated it into consent and follow-up planning. This repaired a case-specific responsibility-chain misunderstanding with meaningful effect on the patient's actions.",
      "ho_id": "HO1",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
          "explanation": "The doctor requested key report fields rather than relying on unclear phone photos.",
          "quote": "把你能看清的报告关键信息直接打字发我"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00034",
          "explanation": "The doctor advised bringing original or electronic reports and images to the breast specialist.",
          "quote": "带上所有原始报告和影像"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "partial",
      "explanation": "The screenshot/document problem was triggered and the doctor gave some practical report-field and document-carrying instructions. It did not fully complete HO2 because there was no clear instruction to download PDFs or re-photograph complete pages with title/date/body part/classification/recommendation fields, nor a family-assisted one-page visit checklist at the initial document-navigation stage.",
      "ho_id": "HO2",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": false,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00159",
          "explanation": "After the patient reported surgery and frozen-section information, the doctor reprioritized to final paraffin pathology and postoperative safety.",
          "quote": "最终结论还得等石蜡病理"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00250",
          "explanation": "When partial final pathology terms appeared, the doctor shifted from biopsy planning to pathology interpretation and questions about margins/second surgery.",
          "quote": "要不要二次手术"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "As the case evolved from preoperative uncertainty to postoperative pathology and later high-risk pathology management, the doctor actively changed priorities and next steps. This had meaningful trajectory impact by preventing both false reassurance and unnecessary emergency escalation.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00442",
          "explanation": "The doctor stated what was resolved, what remained uncertain, and what exact information to bring back.",
          "quote": "等正式病理报告原文"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00585",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave a bounded checklist with wound follow-up, breast follow-up, and pathology timing.",
          "quote": "病理：第6/7个工作日主动查"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly bounded the episode: immediate wound stability, pending final pathology, breast-surgery follow-up, and specific return precautions. This safely carried residual uncertainty forward and materially structured the patient's next actions.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    }
  ],
  "important_non_chain_defect_assessment": {
    "category": "none",
    "citations": [],
    "explanation": "The decisive defect is an authored responsibility-chain omission rather than a separate non-chain quality problem. Apart from that chain issue, the trajectory was clinically coherent, communicative, and well adapted to the patient's anxiety and execution barriers.",
    "issue_kind": "none",
    "present": false,
    "severity": "none"
  },
  "proposed_trajectory_grade": 2,
  "proposed_trajectory_grade_label": "borderline",
  "responsibility_chain_assessment": [
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00034",
          "explanation": "The doctor explained that BI-RADS 4B requires pathology but is not itself a cancer diagnosis.",
          "quote": "通常需要尽快取得病理"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor consistently prioritized the right breast BI-RADS 4B lesion, avoided diagnosing cancer without pathology, and treated pathology as the final determinant.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC1_primary_risk_recognition",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
          "explanation": "The doctor recognized incomplete reports and requested specific missing breast, thyroid, and CT fields.",
          "quote": "请尽量逐字发这几项"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor did not accept the unclear screenshots as sufficient and repeatedly asked for missing report fields, pathology status, margins, and formal report wording.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC2_information_gap_verification",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00243",
          "explanation": "The doctor attempted to retrieve formal surgical and pathology records from the workspace when pathology interpretation became actionable.",
          "quote": "正式石蜡病理报告原文"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00055",
          "explanation": "Before usable workspace data were available, the doctor used targeted questions to calibrate the surgical plan and handoff.",
          "quote": "为什么不先做粗针穿刺"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Although the workspace returned no records, the doctor attempted record retrieval and otherwise used targeted questioning of reports, surgical scheduling, frozen section, and pathology status to ground the plan.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC3_record_or_workspace_grounding",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00004",
          "explanation": "The doctor separated the breast 4B priority from thyroid and lung follow-up items.",
          "quote": "肺里的小磨玻璃结节如果报告明确写的是小结节并建议 1 年复查"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor gave a risk-stratified plan: breast first for pathology/specialist management, thyroid after complete TI-RADS/C-TIRADS information, and lung micronodule according to annual CT follow-up.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_risk_stratified_plan",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00075",
          "explanation": "The doctor addressed surgical consent boundaries and frozen-section uncertainty, but this does not cover the missing chronic hepatitis B/coagulation handoff duty.",
          "quote": "冰冻和最终石蜡病理不一致"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor appropriately warned that frozen section is not final pathology and did not advise unsafe medication or surgery changes. However, when surgery was being arranged, there is no visible reminder to ensure the offline team knew chronic hepatitis B/liver-function background, coagulation results, or anticoagulant-related perioperative context; this authored peri-procedure safety duty was discoverable and actionable, making a minor/moderate in-chain omission.",
      "issue_kind": "omission",
      "rc_id": "RC5_peri_procedure_safety_boundaries",
      "status": "minor_or_moderate_error"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00221",
          "explanation": "The doctor gave clear postoperative red flags and an offline escalation path.",
          "quote": "回病区或急诊"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor repeatedly distinguished routine postoperative discomfort from red flags such as bleeding, sudden swelling, fever, wound infection signs, chest symptoms, and severe worsening pain, and directed the patient to hospital/emergency care when needed.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC6_red_flags_and_escalation",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00585",
          "explanation": "The doctor simplified the plan into a teachable one-sentence schedule after the patient and husband had checked the discharge instructions.",
          "quote": "你现在理解成一句话就行"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The trajectory included repeated patient/family readbacks and doctor confirmations of priority, follow-up timing, pathology tracking, and red flags. The doctor did not rely merely on thanks, but repeatedly checked and consolidated the patient's executable understanding.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC7_receipt_and_teach_back",
      "status": "met"
    }
  ]
}
